onyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:04:24-07:00","id":174924,"title":"","content":"Bit of a different idea: Fairest? Not the most intuitive, but think about it: when he's playing, he certainly draws people in almost like magic, they're frequently tall, good-looking (and he's a very good-looking man), and if we allow the Dancer kith ability to apply to basketball since a lot of the skills are transferable (agility, co-ordination and the like), that works as well.<br /> <br /> Particularly if you imagine his Durance was being forced to play basketball over and over again, with his 'role' being the skilled make-the-winning-shot-in-the-last-two-seconds character, Fairest does actually sort-of work, at least in a messed-up Fae way.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:11:15-07:00","id":174933,"title":"","content":"An excellent point, Allan. Jordan was lionized in the '90s, which seems very much in line with the Fairest, as does people wanting to be 'Like Mike'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[